# Cloudflare Pages _redirects — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Any specific rewrites or redirects go ABOVE the catch-all so they run first.
# Cloudflare processes rules top-to-bottom and stops at the first match.
#
# Methodology content moved into /products bottom section. Preserve old
# links (external bookmarks, search-index results, other-site references).
/methodology         /products#methodology  301
/methodology.html    /products.html#methodology  301
#
# /lookup retired 2026-08-02. A pasted URL gives the server a product
# identifier and nothing else — the page could only answer for products
# already scored by an extension user, or ones Claude happened to
# recognise from a bare id, so it mostly returned "Unknown product" and
# read as "we can't find much". Making it genuinely work would require
# fetching retailer pages server-side, which is specifically what the
# 2026-08-01 legal review told us not to do. Send the traffic to the
# extension, which scores from the user's own browser.
/lookup              /products  301
/lookup.html         /products.html  301
#
# Catch-all 404 for anything not matching a real static file. Without this
# Cloudflare Pages was serving index.html with a 200 status for unknown
# URLs — a soft-404 that confused users and hurt SEO. The `404` status
# code at the end tells CF Pages to serve /404.html with an actual HTTP
# 404 status, which is the correct semantic response.
/*    /404.html    404
